From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: hobot: add vendor IPC header search paths

The Hobot remoteproc driver consumes the shared-memory IPC interface and
the GUA audio IPC wrapper, but its Makefile does not expose either header
directory.  Enabling HOBOT_REMOTEPROC therefore fails at the first include.

Use srctree-relative paths so both in-tree and O= builds resolve the vendor
headers without relying on an absolute build-machine path.
---
 drivers/remoteproc/Makefile | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/Makefile b/drivers/remoteproc/Makefile
index 62ba7e234..51bd8fede 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/Makefile
@@ -41,3 +41,6 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_TI_K3_M4_REMOTEPROC)	+= ti_k3_m4_remoteproc.o ti_k3_common.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TI_K3_R5_REMOTEPROC)	+= ti_k3_r5_remoteproc.o ti_k3_common.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_XLNX_R5_REMOTEPROC)	+= xlnx_r5_remoteproc.o
+ccflags-$(CONFIG_HOBOT_REMOTEPROC) += -I$(srctree)/drivers/mailbox/hobot/ipc/common
+ccflags-$(CONFIG_HOBOT_REMOTEPROC) += -I$(srctree)/sound/soc/gua
+
 obj-$(CONFIG_HOBOT_REMOTEPROC) += hobot_remoteproc.o
-- 
2.51.0
